 cultural ceremonies let graduates recognize achievement alongside communities and traditions meaningful to them.","evidence_claim":"CSULB states that Cultural Graduation Celebrations have been a university tradition for more than three decades and reports nine annual celebrations during commencement season.","source_url":"https://www.csulb.edu/news/article/csulbs-cultural-celebrations-honor-graduates-identities-and-heritages-0","source_title":"CSULB's Cultural Celebrations honor graduates' identities and heritages","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2024-05-29","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The celebrations are voluntary; event-specific registration, costs, attire, and guest rules vary and must be checked on current Student Affairs pages.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"long-beach-state-dirtbags-nickname","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Long Beach State Dirtbags Nickname","title":"Call the Baseball Team the Dirtbags","subtitle":"The one team nickname exempted from Beach Athletics naming rules","notes":"Use “Dirtbags” specifically for Long Beach State baseball, and connect it to the 1989 team’s all-dirt practice-field story.","short_summary":"Baseball alone carries the Dirtbags name, rooted in an improvised 1989 season and a dirt-covered style of play.","evidence_claim":"Long Beach State Athletics calls Dirtbags its baseball team’s longstanding informal nickname and traces it to the 1989 team, whose infielders practiced on an all-dirt field.","source_url":"https://longbeachstate.com/sports/2018/8/1/_trads_traditions_html","source_title":"List of Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2018-08-01","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This naming tradition belongs specifically to Long Beach State baseball; other varsity teams use Beach Athlet